(I)--(alias उशनस्) a son of Kavi (हविर्धान and दिव्या, hence काव्य); married ऊर्जस्वती, and father of [page३-439+ ४९] देवयानी through जयन्ती.
1: भा. III. 1. २२; IV. 1. ४५; V. 1. ३५; VI. 7. १८; वा. ६३. २३; ६५. ७४; ९३. ८५; १०१. ३३; Vi. I, १४. 2.
The Purohita of हिरण्यकशिपु. Father of शण्ड and Marka, tutors of प्रह्लाद. Took part in प्रह्लाद's coronation. A ब्रह्मऋषि: Heard of the in- sult offered to his daughter by शर्मिष्ठा, the daughter of the ruler वृषपर्वन् and left the capital. The Purohita of वृषपर्वन्, the latter made him stay offering to make his daughter a slave of देवयाणी. In offering the latter to ययाति, he asked him not to share his bed with शर्मिष्ठा, cursed ययाति to become aged for having shared his bed with शर्मिष्ठा, and on an appeal mitigated it by saying that he could exchange his old age with youth of another if he found one to accept the exchange;
2: भा. IX. Ch. १८ (whole); VII. 5. 1-2 १०. ३३; Br. III. ६८. १५; M. २५. 4, १६; २७. २६, ३७; ३०. ३०-36; ३२. २३, २६; ३३. 2 and २६.
joined Soma in तारकामय war: blessed the Asuras in this war: fought with बृहस्पति in a देवासुर battle.
3: भा. IX. १४. 6; VIII. १०. ३३.
Brought back to life the unconscious Bali by सञ्जीविनी Vidya. Presented Bali with an unfading garland of flowers; knowing वामन to be Hari, warned Bali from agreeing to his request. Bali would not hear, and शुक्र cursed him to lose all श्री. At the bidding of Hari com- pleted the यज्ञ begun by Bali.
4: Ib. VIII. ११. ४७-8; १५. 6; १९. ३०-43; २०. 1-१५; २३. १८; Br. III. ३०. ५४; ६५. ३१; M. १९२. १०; २४६. 1.
The third वेदव्यास. Heard the पुराण from वायु and told it to बृहस्पति;
5: Br. III. 1. ७६ and ८६; १०. १८; II. ३५. ११७; IV. 4. ५९.
wor- shipped स्थानु with severe penance; born in तिष्यनक्षत्र: married mind-born daughter of पितृस् (Somapas) and father of 4 sons, त्वष्ट्रि, Varatri, शण्ड and Marka;
6: Ib. I. 1. १२७-9; II. २४. ५०-51 and १३१; ३३. ३२; III. 1. ७५-8; १०. ८६-7; ६८. १५, ८६-7.
cursed the Asuras when they lost their empire, and यज्ञ came to the side of Devas. Asura's appeal and शुक्र's penance to शिव. Finding the Asuras having no आचार्य, the Devas attacked them who appealed to शुक्र's mother. विष्णु at the instance of Indra slew her, a woman and a wife of भृगु, for which विष्णु was cursed to be born on earth as man seven times. Indra then set up his daughter जयन्ती to serve शुक्र and earn his goodwill. Pleased with her service, शुक्र agreed to live with her as husband for ten years. After this period, बृहस्पति assumed his form and deluded the Asuras. शुक्र who grew angry cursed the Asuras at which बृहस्पति felt happy and threw off his disguise. They appealed to शुक्र for help once again or threatened to leave for रसातलम्. He managed to get back their kingdom in the epoch of सावर्णि [page३-440+ ४८] when Bali was emperor;
7: Ib. III. ७२. ९३-195; ७३. 2, ५८; M. ४७. ८६-111, १७२-202.
lives in Bhuvarlokam; आश्रम of, located below the सहस्रशिखर and Kumuda hills;
8: Br. IV. 2. ३०; वा. ३८. ६०-2;
consecrated भण्ड on the throne;
9: Br. IV. १२ 2-6; १७. ५६.
